#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:5
#: aa395544af554a9fa3fd546f15b4f37a
msgid "Tuning Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:7
#: 4cc09c9d94bb4548a0d267732e27b342
msgid "This page describes how to tune the Navigation control including the \"L1 controller\".  The lower level :ref:`speed <rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed>` and :ref:`turn rate <rover-tuning-steering-rate>` controllers should be tuned before attempting to tune this controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:13
#: 093bd3bb3e0848089ce89aa876bf69ef
msgid "L1 controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:15
#: 27286888ff984e4194f4780f6990932c
msgid "The L1 one controller is the highest level steering controller.  It accepts position targets (i.e. latitude, longitude points) and the vehicle's current speed and outputs a desired lateral acceleration which is then fed into lower level controllers (including the Steering Rate controller).  Together this leads to the vehicle tracking a line towards the target.  This controller is used in all the autonomous modes including :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>`, :ref:`Guided <guided-mode>`, :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` and :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:17
#: 8564585cd4fa418aa78b0e3a007c34f4
msgid "Recommended steps for tuning the L1 controller:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:19
#: 48062c4132d04c70963647ce381e4967
msgid "Connect the ground station to the vehicle using a telemetry radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:20
#: 2b3cbd5030794fc78364bb89afe005f5
msgid "Create an rectangular or back-and-forth mission (perhaps using the Mission Planner's Flight Plan screen) and upload to the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:21
#: a728b5d71faf4556bb0371936d0f7caf
msgid "Arm the vehicle (in :ref:`Manual <manual-mode>` or :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>`) and switch to :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:22
#: 47d320bbe3324004973de9c1071abf8f
msgid "If the rover weaves along the straights, then raise :ref:`NAVL1_PERIOD <NAVL1_PERIOD>` (aka \"Lat Acc Cntrl Period\") in increments of 0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:23
#: f1aebc011ac74e04bc152699cedc453f
msgid "If the rover does not turn sharply enough then lower :ref:`NAVL1_PERIOD <NAVL1_PERIOD>` (aka \"Lat Acc Cntrl Period\") in increments of 0.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:24
#: 2f12a4b5f2da427789b5b5591cb787d7
msgid "Raise :ref:`NAVL1_DAMPING <NAVL1_DAMPING>` (aka \"Lat Acc Cntrl Damp\") by increments of 0.05 to improve navigation in tight courses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:30
#: 3ead6028bbe54397a59f1d70fa021be4
msgid "Other Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:32
#: 44f454eb2a994aa48c60f80be54444b7
msgid ":ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G <ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` defines the maximum lateral acceleration (in Gs = 9.81m/s/s) the controllers will attempt during cornering.  Most vehicles cannot achieve more than 0.3G.  To more precisely measure the vehicle's maximum possible lateral acceleration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:34
#: 9f5f57f7a1e140028d7788c7be7ee230
msgid "On Mission Planner's Flight Data screen, check the \"Tuning\" checkbox (bottom middle), double click on the graph and select \"ay\" (Acceleration Y-axis)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:35
#: 812fbbcdda0d4a2dba227d4b01d22fd1
msgid "Drive the vehicle in Manual mode at a high speed making very sharp turns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:36
#: 47cf687f9f5a47a3a09629084a582e3e
msgid "Set :ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G <ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` to slightly lower than the highest values seen.  Note the value shown may be in cm/s/s so the value should be divided by 981 to match the parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:38
#: 9f4c813fff8c448f8a71699a1c21a347
msgid ":ref:`WP_SPEED <WP_SPEED>` defines the target speed (in m/s) that the vehicle will drive at in :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>` and :ref:`Guided <guided-mode>`.  It will also be used in :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` and :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` if :ref:`RTL_SPEED <RTL_SPEED>` is set to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:39
#: de336e824336407c99d08741f3111c1b
msgid ":ref:`WP_RADIUS <WP_RADIUS>` specifies the distance before the waypoint that the vehicle may begin turning towards the next waypoint.  This parameter should not be set too low or the vehicle may attempt unhelpful turns as it gets very close to the waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:40
#: 6657389e4542467d983b500d0347d670
msgid "``WP_OVERSHOOT`` is used to slow the vehicle if it strays too far from the line between the origin and destination.  If set too low the vehicle may slow down very often as its position drfits off the line between waypoints.  If set too high the vehicle may not slow down for corners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-navigation-420.rst:41
#: b0f62804ce9e40eaa8f4598275510999
msgid ":ref:`PIVOT_TURN_ANGLE <PIVOT_TURN_ANGLE>` is only used by skid steering vehicles.  If the vehicle's heading error becomes larger than this value (in degrees) the vehicle will momentarily stop and pivot towards the target before continuing.  See :ref:`Tuning Pivot Turns <rover-tuning-pivot-turns>` for more details."
msgstr ""
